// A `char` or `bool` result travels in a whole register, so Ghidra returns it
// as an extension of the narrow value through a register-sized varnode.
// Narrowing that back to the declared return type gives the same value, so it
// is not a narrowed return.
//
//   zext_byte, sext_byte   a byte extended to 4 bytes, returned as a byte
//   zext_bool              a bool extended to 4 bytes, returned as a bool
//
// The extension only helps when the value it extends fits the return type:
//
//   zext_short_as_byte     a 16-bit value returned as a byte loses its high half
//   zext_byte_as_bool      a byte may be 2, which a bool return turns into 1
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: grep -c "return-narrowed" %t.log | %file-check -check-prefix=COUNT %s
//
// WARN-DAG: lossy lift [return-narrowed]: 32-bit returned value truncated to the declared 8-bit return type 'unsigned char' in function 'zext_short_as_byte'
// WARN-DAG: lossy lift [return-narrowed]: 32-bit returned value reduced to a truth value by the declared return type '_Bool' in function 'zext_byte_as_bool'
// The other three functions are not reported.
